#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "Listen address (`http.host`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default bind is `127.0.0.1:2658` (loopback only). For LAN access via `http://<PC-IP>:2658/web` or a local hostname such as `http://galaxy:2658/web`, set:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:49
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"http:\n"
"  host: 0.0.0.0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:55
msgid ""
"Multiple binds (distinct interfaces only — not client-facing aliases). Use "
"`0.0.0.0` instead of listing every IP; do not mix `0.0.0.0` with specific "
"addresses. Hostnames must resolve on the Hub machine (`/etc/hosts` or DNS):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"http:\n"
"  host:\n"
"    - 127.0.0.1\n"
"    - 10.244.0.2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:64
msgid ""
"CLI `--host` overrides config for a single run / systemd unit write. After "
"changing `http.host`, run `anima service restart`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without Tunnel, LAN: `http://<PC-IP>:2658/web/chat` with `http.host: 0.0.0.0` (or `anima service start --host 0.0.0.0`); clients set Hub URL to `http://<PC-IP>:2658` (no `/web` suffix).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-origin (`http.cors_origins`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:70
msgid ""
"When the browser UI and Hub API share the same origin (default: `https://"
"anima.example.com/web` + `https://anima.example.com/api`), **no CORS config "
"is needed**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:72
msgid ""
"Add origins only for **cross-origin** cases (e.g. Vite dev server, external "
"reverse proxy splitting UI and API):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:73
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"http:\n"
"  cors_origins:\n"
"    - http://127.0.0.1:4173\n"
msgstr ""
"http:\n"
"  cors_origins:\n"
"    - http://127.0.0.1:4173\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:80
msgid "CORS is **not** derived from `tunnel` or `web.public_url`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Tunnel (optional)"
msgstr "2. Tunnel（可选）"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:83
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"anima tunnel setup\n"
"anima service start\n"
msgstr ""
"anima tunnel setup\n"
"anima service start\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:89
msgid ""
"When `tunnel.enabled: true`, cloudflared starts with **`anima service "
"start`** stack (no separate `anima-tunnel.service`). Ingress points to Hub "
"`:2658` only; Web UI is served at **`/web`** on the same hostname."
msgstr ""
"当 `tunnel.enabled: true` 时，cloudflared 随 **`anima service start`** 栈启动"
"（无独立 `anima-tunnel.service`）。Ingress 默认指向本地 Hub `:2658`；配置 "
"`tunnel.web_hostname` 与 `web.enabled` 时，第二条 ingress 指向 Web `:2659`。"

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"tunnel:\n"
"  enabled: true\n"
"  hostname: anima.example.com\n"
"\n"
"web:\n"
"  enabled: true\n"
"  public_url: https://anima.example.com/web\n"
msgstr ""
"tunnel:\n"
"  enabled: true\n"
"  hostname: anima.example.com\n"
"  web_hostname: app.anima.example.com\n"
"\n"
"web:\n"
"  enabled: true\n"
"  port: 2659\n"
"  public_url: https://app.anima.example.com\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:101
msgid ""
"Browser: `https://anima.example.com/web/chat` · Hub API: `https://"
"anima.example.com/api`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/remote-access.md:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without Tunnel, LAN: `http://<PC-IP>:2658/web/chat` with `http.host: 0.0.0.0` in config (see above); clients set Hub URL to `http://<PC-IP>:2658` (no `/web` suffix).\n"
msgstr ""

